# Verify gates

## Honesty (mandatory)

- Never claim tests passed unless you ran them.
- If not run, say so explicitly.
- Prefer the **smallest relevant** check (`pytest path::test`) before full gate.
- Do not expand test scope unless the task requires it.
- Do not create **new test files** without explicit user/job approval.

Policy: [docs/agent-testing-policy.md](mdc:docs/agent-testing-policy.md). Guard: `scripts/guard_new_tests.py`.

## Commands

| Scope | Command |
| ----- | ------- |
| Python lint | `ruff check .` |
| Python types | `mypy src` |
| Python format check | `black --check .` |
| Python tests | `pytest` or `pytest path::test` |
| Full gate | `python scripts/verify_phase_completion.py` (9 steps; exe smoke if `dist/` built) |
| Beta smokes only | `python scripts/beta_gate.py` |
| Web lint | `cd web && npm run lint` |

Report in job output: each command, exit status, and brief failure excerpt.

## When to run what

- Docs-only: usually skip code gates; state skipped.
- `src/` / `tests/`: ruff + mypy + targeted pytest minimum.
- `web/**`: add `npm run lint`; add tests only if job or user requires.
- Pre-PR / release jobs: full gate script.
